       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">POSITIVE</span> · The Better India · 2026-11-01 · editor 10/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>85-year-old Kerala woman teaches children using sand</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#positive</span> <span>#brief</span></div>
       <p>Indira Amma, an 85-year-old from Kerala, is teaching children Malayalam, Hindi, English, and mathematics using a traditional method involving sand and a stick. Drawing on the cultural ritual of Ezhuthiniruthu, she helps young learners trace letters in sand to build familiarity through touch and repetition. This approach serves as an experiential alternative to modern digital tools.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-11-01/85-year-old-kerala-woman-teaches-children-using-sand.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>For the past decade, Amma has mentored children at the Temple of English School, emphasizing patience and consistency. Her practice highlights the value of traditional, low-cost educational methods that allow children to learn at their own pace while connecting with Kerala’s cultural heritage.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The brief accurately summarizes the method and context provided in the source.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
