     <article class="story single" data-beat="national">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">NATIONAL</span> · The Hindu · 2026-11-01 · editor 10/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>Avarekai cultivation in Kolar district drops by 70% due to drought</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#national</span> <span>#brief</span></div>
       <p>Avarekai cultivation in Karnataka's Kolar district has plummeted by 70% this season, falling from 1,000 hectares to just 300 hectares. The Department of Agriculture attributes this sharp decline to deficient rainfall, depleting groundwater levels, and persistent dry weather which discouraged farmers from sowing.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-11-01/avarekai-cultivation-in-kolar-district-drops-by-70-due-to-dr.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>Agricultural experts warn that the reduced harvest may significantly impact supply to Bengaluru markets. With peak consumption season approaching for festivals like Sankranti, retail prices for the popular field beans could climb to ₹100 per kg. Currently, fresh Avarekai is retailing between ₹80 and ₹88 per kg in Bengaluru.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The brief is accurate, dense, and summarizes all key figures and context from the source text perfectly.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://www.thehindu.com/news/national/karnataka/avarekai-cultivation-in-kolar-district-drops-by-70-amid-rainfall-deficit/article71653287.ece" rel="noopener">The Hindu</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       
