     <article class="story single" data-beat="finance">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">FINANCE</span> · Livemint Money · 2026-11-01 · editor 10/10 · 2 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>EPFO Launches WhatsApp Services for PF Balance, Passbook Access</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#Personal Finance</span> <span>#EPFO</span> <span>#WhatsApp</span> <span>#PF Balance</span></div>
       <p>The Employees’ Provident Fund Organisation (EPFO) has rolled out new WhatsApp-based services, making it significantly easier for its subscribers to access provident fund account information and resolve compliance-related issues without the need to visit EPFO offices. Union Labour and Employment Minister Mansukh Mandaviya officially launched this facility on November 1, 2026, during the EPFO's 74th Foundation Day celebrations held in New Delhi. This initiative is designed to leverage a widely used mobile platform to enhance the accessibility of routine provident fund services for millions of members, according to Livemint Money.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-11-01/epfo-launches-whatsapp-services-for-pf-balance-passbook-acce.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>Subscribers can now check their PF balance, retrieve information from their passbooks, and view their latest five transactions directly through EPFO's verified WhatsApp service. Beyond these core functions, the facility will also offer personalized guidance and assistance to members who need to complete requirements under the Pradhan Mantri Viksit Bharat Rozgar Yojana (PMVBRY). This PMVBRY-related support is particularly beneficial for those members whose benefits or compliance needs are pending due to issues like incomplete Aadhaar authentication or other documentation-related concerns, streamlining processes that previously might have required multiple platform logins or physical visits.</p><p>To access these new services, members are advised to use only the WhatsApp contact details published on EPFO's official website or other verified communication channels. While the November 1 launch announcement did not specify the official WhatsApp number or a step-by-step activation process, Minister Mandaviya had indicated in May 2026 that members would be able to initiate conversations by sending a 'Hello' message to the EPFO's verified number. The proposed service is also expected to support regional languages and provide automated responses around the clock, further enhancing user convenience. It is crucial for members to exercise caution and avoid sharing sensitive information such as their UAN password, OTP, Aadhaar details, or bank credentials with unverified numbers.</p><p>This WhatsApp launch is part of EPFO's broader strategic efforts to improve access to provident fund services through technological advancements. At the same Foundation Day event, Minister Mandaviya also introduced an automatic settlement facility for eligible inoperative EPF accounts that hold balances of up to ₹1,000. Under this initiative, members with Aadhaar-verified inoperative accounts will no longer be required to file individual claims. Instead, the EPFO will proactively initiate the settlement process after prescribed identity and bank-account verifications, subsequently transferring eligible dues to the rightful beneficiaries. This move is anticipated to benefit approximately one lakh accounts, involving a total of ₹5 crore. The EPFO currently serves an extensive base of approximately 8 crore contributory members and 85 lakh pensioners, managing a retirement corpus of nearly ₹32 lakh crore. The organization also reported a significant improvement in its average claim settlement time, which declined to 2.57 days in October 2026, reflecting the efficacy of its technology-enabled claim-processing systems. The WhatsApp facility is expected to particularly benefit subscribers who may find EPFO's existing digital platforms challenging to navigate.</p><p>What to watch: The official rollout of the WhatsApp number and further digital enhancements.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The draft is comprehensive, well-structured, and includes all relevant figures and context provided in the source text.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
