     <article class="story single" data-beat="cricket">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">CRICKET</span> · Crictracker · 2026-11-01 · editor 9/10 · 2 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>Gambhir Backs Shreyas Iyer After India's 3-2 T20I Series Win Over New Zealand</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#Cricket</span> <span>#India</span> <span>#New Zealand</span> <span>#T20I Series</span></div>
       <p>India secured a 3-2 series victory against New Zealand in the T20I series, winning the opening three matches before the hosts claimed the final two encounters at Hamilton on November 1, 2026. Head coach Gautam Gambhir lauded the team's aggressive approach and resilience, especially given the minimal preparation time the squad had upon arriving in unfamiliar conditions.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-11-01/gambhir-backs-shreyas-iyer-after-indias-3-2-t20i-series-win-.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>The team's demanding schedule saw them compete in the Asian Games in Japan from September 24 to October 3, 2026, where they clinched a gold medal. This was immediately followed by a five-match T20I series against West Indies from October 6 to October 17, 2026. India then touched down in New Zealand on October 20, 2026, managed just one day of practice on October 21, and commenced their first T20I match on October 22.</p><p>Gambhir reflected on the team's performance, stating, &quot;Biggest achievement, apart from winning, is how they've handled the conditions and how ruthless they were in the first three games.&quot; He emphasized the &quot;incredible effort because the boys got only one day to prepare,&quot; highlighting the challenges of different conditions, weather, dimensions, and playing against a quality New Zealand side with limited experience in their backyard, especially for many touring New Zealand for the first time.</p><p>India's aggressive intent was evident in the opening T20I, where they successfully chased 225 runs. Notable contributions came from Shreyas Iyer, who scored 28 off 42 balls, and Naman Dhir, who added 42 off just 15 deliveries. The second T20I presented a tougher challenge, with India reduced to 70 for 5, before Tilak Varma, Naman Dhir, and Nitish Reddy guided the chase to victory. India completed the pursuit of 199 runs in a mere 13.2 overs, exemplifying the ruthlessness Gambhir referenced.</p><p>Gambhir also addressed Shreyas Iyer's captaincy, noting that he took over a &quot;very, very successful T20 team&quot; that had won the World Cup and remained unbeaten in series play for two years. The coach acknowledged the significant challenge of building a new squad while maintaining such a winning record, particularly with an inexperienced bowling attack. He stressed the importance of developing young players through exposure on the road as the team prepares for the next World Cup cycle.</p><p>Iyer's captaincy tenure prior to this series included defeats to Ireland and England, followed by victories in Zimbabwe and Afghanistan, and the gold medal triumph at the Asian Games in Japan. The West Indies series concluded in a 2-2 draw. Despite these earlier outcomes, Gambhir expressed strong confidence in his captain's ability to manage the transition effectively. He concluded by saying, &quot;Shreyas has done a fabulous job, with so much of inexperience in the bowling lineup. Because as a captain, you're only as good as how your bowlers or your batters perform. Especially with an inexperienced attack, I think he's done a phenomenal job.&quot;</p><p>What to watch: The continued development of young players under Iyer's captaincy ahead of the next World Cup cycle.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The draft successfully synthesizes the coach's comments with the series timeline and context, accurately reflecting the team's performance and the captaincy transition.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://www.crictracker.com/cricket-news/shreyas-has-done-a-fabulous-job-gautam-gambhir-backs-india-t20i-captain-after-3-2-series-win-8462/" rel="noopener">Crictracker</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       
