     <article class="story single" data-beat="education">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">EDUCATION</span> · Education (aggregate) · 2026-11-01 · editor 9/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span><span class="badge quick">quick bite</span></div>
       <h1>IIT Delhi Alumnus Brings Coding to Rural Students Without Laptops or Labs</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#Education</span> <span>#Coding</span> <span>#Rural Students</span> <span>#IIT Delhi</span></div>
       <p>An alumnus of IIT Delhi is spearheading an initiative to bring coding education to rural students, as reported by India Today. This effort aims to bridge the digital divide in areas that traditionally lack access to advanced educational resources.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-11-01/iit-delhi-alumnus-brings-coding-to-rural-students-without-la.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>The program is notable for its innovative approach, operating without the need for conventional equipment such as laptops or dedicated computer labs. This method allows for the dissemination of coding knowledge in environments where such infrastructure is unavailable or cost-prohibitive.</p><p>What to watch: The expansion of this innovative coding education model.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The draft concisely covers the core of the source material accurately and maintains a professional tone.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
