     <article class="story single" data-beat="world">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">WORLD</span> · The Hindu World · 2026-11-01 · editor 9/10 · 2 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>Jaishankar Holds Bilateral Talks at G20 Foreign Ministers' Meeting in Atlanta</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#Diplomacy</span> <span>#G20</span> <span>#S. Jaishankar</span> <span>#World Affairs</span></div>
       <p>External Affairs Minister S. Jaishankar engaged in a series of separate bilateral meetings with his Russian, Polish, and South Korean counterparts in the U.S. on Saturday, October 31, 2026. These crucial discussions took place on the sidelines of the G20 Foreign Ministers' Meeting in Atlanta, where a broad agenda encompassing the Ukraine conflict, the evolving situation in West Asia, bilateral ties, and multilateral issues was addressed, as reported by The Hindu World.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-11-01/jaishankar-holds-bilateral-talks-at-g20-foreign-ministers-me.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>In his interaction with Russian Foreign Minister Sergey Lavrov, Mr. Jaishankar conveyed on social media that they &quot;discussed the Ukraine conflict, Gulf situation and multilateral issues.&quot; Similarly, the External Affairs Minister met Polish Deputy Prime Minister and Foreign Minister Radoslaw Sikorski. Their discussions, as noted by Mr. Jaishankar, &quot;focused on the Ukraine conflict, India-EU ties and the G20.&quot; Poland is attending this year's G20 meetings as a full participant, following an invitation from the U.S., and has also expressed a clear interest in securing permanent membership of the grouping. Meanwhile, the G20 foreign ministers' talks in Atlanta were overshadowed by divisions over Russia’s war with Ukraine, leading U.S. Secretary of State Marco Rubio to prepare a chairman’s statement instead of a joint communique.</p><p>Mr. Jaishankar also held a meeting with South Korean Foreign Minister Cho Hyun. He &quot;appreciated the stocktaking with @FMChoHyun of the Republic of Korea of our bilateral cooperation, as also the discussion on G20 and multilateral issues,&quot; he stated. Additionally, the External Affairs Minister met his Canadian counterpart, Anita Anand, in Atlanta. Both ministers concurred that Prime Minister Modi’s Canada visit in December would serve as &quot;another building block&quot; in strengthening bilateral relations.</p><p>Following two days of intensive brainstorming on global affairs, Mr. Jaishankar and his fellow G20 foreign ministers partook in a distinctly American experience. They attended a college football game between the Florida Gators and the Georgia Bulldogs at the Mercedes-Benz Stadium in Atlanta. Secretary Rubio, who escorted the visitors, posted on social media that he was &quot;Happy to introduce my fellow foreign ministers to the quintessential American sport of football and welcome them to #GatorNation.&quot; Notably, Mr. Rubio's son Anthony plays as a running back for the Florida Gators and is in his fourth season. Prior to this, Secretary Rubio had also remarked that the Quad group was &quot;delivering results for people in Indo-Pacific,&quot; reviewing progress in turning shared priorities into real benefits for the region.</p><p>What to watch: The outcomes of the G20 discussions and upcoming diplomatic engagements.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The draft effectively synthesizes the provided full text and accurately reports the diplomatic engagements and the football game anecdote.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://www.thehindu.com/news/international/s-jaishankar-meets-russian-polish-south-korean-counterparts-discusses-ukraine-west-asia/article71653057.ece" rel="noopener">The Hindu World</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       
