     <article class="story single" data-beat="entertainment">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">ENTERTAINMENT</span> · TOI Entertainment · 2026-11-01 · editor 10/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>Kanye West Sells Stripped-Down Malibu Home After Abandoned Renovation</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#entertainment</span> <span>#brief</span></div>
       <p>Kanye West has sold his Tadao Ando-designed Malibu home for $21 million to developer Steven 'Bo' Belmont. West purchased the beachfront property for $57.25 million in 2021 with plans to build a minimalist bunker, but the home was stripped to its concrete core before being abandoned amid financial losses and lawsuits.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-11-01/kanye-west-sells-stripped-down-malibu-home-after-abandoned-r.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>Belmont is now leading an $8.5 million restoration project to return the structure to its original state. West’s interest in Ando’s work previously led him to briefly occupy a separate $200 million Malibu estate, which was later acquired by Jay-Z and Beyoncé in a record-breaking off-market transaction.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The brief accurately synthesizes the complex timeline of the two Malibu properties and the ownership transitions mentioned in the source.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
