       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">NATIONAL</span> · India Today · 2026-11-01 · editor 9/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>Karnataka CM DK Shivakumar Pursues Official Status for Kannada Flag</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#national</span> <span>#brief</span></div>
       <p>Karnataka Chief Minister DK Shivakumar has announced his government's commitment to granting official state status to the Kannada flag. The administration aims to mandate that the flag be hoisted alongside the National Flag on all government buildings across the state. Shivakumar plans to introduce a legal framework and pass an official resolution to formalize this practice during the upcoming Belagavi Assembly session.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-11-01/karnataka-cm-dk-shivakumar-pursues-official-status-for-kanna.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>While the state Cabinet previously sought recognition for the flag from the Central Government, the request was not approved. The Chief Minister intends to revisit the issue through new legislative discussions and Cabinet deliberations, framing the initiative as a government priority requiring public participation.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The brief accurately summarizes the government's stance and the legislative process described in the source.</p>
