     <article class="story single" data-beat="positive">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">POSITIVE</span> · The Better India · 2026-11-01 · editor 10/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>Miss India Finalist Defies Bullying Over Birthmark</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#Miss India Uttar Pradesh</span> <span>#Port-Wine Stain</span> <span>#Birthmark Awareness</span> <span>#Self-Love</span></div>
       <p>A Miss India Uttar Pradesh finalist, born with a port-wine stain on her face, has transformed her journey from enduring cruel comments and bullying to becoming an inspiration. Despite being told, “Nobody can love that face,” she now stands as a testament to self-acceptance, recently winning the People's Choice Award.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-11-01/miss-india-finalist-defies-bullying-over-birthmark.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>Growing up, she faced relentless stares and taunts, with children refusing to sit with her at school, causing deep emotional hurt. This led her to skip school, avoid photographs, and hide from others, reaching a point where she could not even look at herself in the mirror.</p><p>The turning point came with her sister's encouragement to step in front of a camera, an act that initially terrified her. With her sister's support, she gradually began creating content and exploring modeling. Even in the face of online trolls calling her ugly, she stopped trying to conform to others' definitions of beauty.</p><p>Today, the girl who once avoided cameras is celebrated not for overcoming a visible difference, but for refusing to let prejudice dictate her worth. Her journey has inspired others to embrace themselves, reinforcing her message that no one should ever have to hide their face.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The draft effectively synthesizes the personal narrative from the source without adding external information or inventing details.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://thebetterindia.com/videos/lifestyle/bullied-for-her-birthmark-now-a-miss-india-finalist-12774176" rel="noopener">The Better India</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       
