     <article class="story single" data-beat="sports">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">SPORTS</span> · BBC Sport · 2026-11-01 · editor 10/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>Namibia Secures ODI Series Win Against Ireland</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#sports</span> <span>#brief</span></div>
       <p>Namibia claimed a 3-2 series victory after defeating Ireland by five wickets in the final one-day international in Windhoek. Ireland was bowled out for 129 in 33.1 overs, with JJ Smit taking four wickets for 20 runs. Namibia successfully chased the target in 21.2 overs, led by Louren Steenkamp’s 44.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-11-01/namibia-secures-odi-series-win-against-ireland.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>Ireland captain Lorcan Tucker acknowledged the team's disappointment but emphasized the value of the experience ahead of next year's Cricket World Cup qualifiers. Tucker noted that Namibia outplayed his side through superior intensity and skill execution, providing a lesson for Ireland in managing middle-order batting and bowling phases effectively.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: Succinct and accurate coverage of the series result and the captain's post-match comments.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://www.bbc.co.uk/sport/cricket/articles/cmed34zjq9d5o?at_medium=RSS&amp;at_campaign=rss" rel="noopener">BBC Sport</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       
