       <h1>Nilekani Task Force to Submit Exam Reform Report by January 2027</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#Education</span> <span>#India Today</span> <span>#Exam Reform</span></div>
       <p>A task force led by Nandan Nilekani has been given a specific deadline of January 2027 to submit its comprehensive report on exam reform, as reported by India Today. The group's mandate involves a thorough review and the formulation of proposed changes to the existing examination system. This initiative underscores a significant effort towards modernizing educational assessment in the country. </p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-11-01/nilekani-task-force-to-submit-exam-reform-report-by-january-.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>The January 2027 deadline provides a clear timeframe for the completion and submission of these crucial recommendations, indicating a structured approach to addressing potential overhauls in the education sector. The Nilekani-led task force is expected to deliver its findings within this stipulated period.</p><p>What to watch: The specifics of the proposed exam reforms.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The draft accurately captures the core information provided in the summary, including the task force leader and the deadline.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
