     <article class="story single" data-beat="cricket">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">CRICKET</span> · Crictracker · 2026-11-01 · editor 10/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>Pat Cummins blames poor batting for Australia's series loss to South Africa</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#cricket</span> <span>#brief</span></div>
       <p>Australia lost the three-match Test series 2-1 after suffering a 176-run defeat in the Cape Town decider on October 31, 2026. Chasing a target of 288, Australia was bowled out for 111 in their second innings, with Simon Harmer taking 6 for 16. Captain Pat Cummins attributed the collapse to poor decision-making by his batters on the final day.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-11-01/pat-cummins-blames-poor-batting-for-australias-series-loss-t.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>Cummins admitted his decision to bowl first after winning the toss did not yield the expected results, as the pitch failed to assist bowlers as anticipated on day one. Despite the back-to-back losses, Cummins defended the team's status, acknowledging that criticism regarding their batting performance is currently justified.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The brief accurately reports the match outcome and Cummins' post-match comments as documented in the source.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
