     <article class="story single" data-beat="national">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">NATIONAL</span> · India Today · 2026-11-01 · editor 9/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>Three Arrested for Khalistani Graffiti Targeting Diljit Dosanjh</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#national</span> <span>#brief</span></div>
       <p>Delhi Police have arrested three individuals for painting pro-Khalistani slogans targeting singer Diljit Dosanjh at two Delhi Metro stations. The graffiti, found at Jahangirpuri and Shastri Nagar stations, threatened the artist and called for revenge on behalf of the banned group Sikhs for Justice (SFJ). </p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-11-01/three-arrested-for-khalistani-graffiti-targeting-diljit-dosa.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>Investigators identified the suspects—Sumit, Sumit Kumar, and Gurpreet—after reviewing CCTV footage and tracking encrypted communications. The accused admitted to being hired by SFJ-linked handlers to perform the act for money. Police are currently working to identify the specific handlers who provided the designs and coordinated the operation during Dosanjh's recent concert tour.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: Covers the arrests and the methodology of the accused accurately based on the source text.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://www.indiatoday.in/india/story/diljit-dosanjh-pro-khalistani-slogans-delhi-metro-three-arrested-concert-special-cell-3030166-2026-11-01?utm_source=rss" rel="noopener">India Today</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       
