     <article class="story single" data-beat="national">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">NATIONAL</span> · The Hindu · 2026-11-01 · editor 10/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>West Bengal Notifies Jobs for Families of Political Violence Victims</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#national</span> <span>#brief</span></div>
       <p>The West Bengal government has issued a notification offering Group D government jobs to one family member of individuals killed in political violence since 2001. Announced by Chief Minister Suvendu Adhikari, the scheme serves as a one-time exception to standard recruitment procedures for families impacted over the past 25 years.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-11-01/west-bengal-notifies-jobs-for-families-of-political-violence.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>Eligibility requires the family's monthly income to be below ₹50,000, with applicants submitting FIRs, death certificates, and relationship verification. A screening committee led by District Magistrates and Superintendents of Police will evaluate claims. This policy applies to spouses, children, or third-gender dependents of victims, regardless of the political administration in power during the incident.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The brief accurately reflects the notification details and eligibility criteria mentioned in the source.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://www.thehindu.com/news/national/west-bengal/west-bengal-government-notifies-jobs-for-kin-of-those-killed-in-political-violence/article71653803.ece" rel="noopener">The Hindu</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
